WEBVTT

00:00:00.010 --> 00:00:10.010
= Watch Free Movies On asiankh.org =

00:00:30.875 --> 00:00:34.708
- Dante!
- Dante!

00:01:36.708 --> 00:01:38.625
One, two, three.

00:01:39.916 --> 00:01:40.833
One…

00:02:02.625 --> 00:02:05.083
Come on! Come on, baby, come on!

00:02:32.208 --> 00:02:33.624
Hey, Mom.

00:02:33.625 --> 00:02:36.749
At first I couldn't sleep all night,
I was so excited,

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:38.499
and then I overslept.

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:39.665
No big deal.

00:02:39.666 --> 00:02:42.624
I hope you have
a really, really good first day, sweetie.

00:02:42.625 --> 00:02:43.708
Thanks.

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:47.957
And, you know,
Dad would be so proud of you.

00:02:47.958 --> 00:02:50.499
You're the first woman mechanic
at Eagle Racing.

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:53.958
I have to hang up, I'm nearly there.
Love you. See you later.

00:03:03.416 --> 00:03:06.458
Eagle Headquarters.
You have reached your destination.

00:03:11.916 --> 00:03:15.916
Hey, watch out!
Are you blind or something, you moron?

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:20.250
Sorry, Mr. Annunziata!

00:03:20.791 --> 00:03:21.833
I'm sorry.

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:31.665
Hey, Dante, where are you?

00:03:31.666 --> 00:03:33.957
Have you seen the videos
from last night yet?

00:03:33.958 --> 00:03:35.957
Because people will be talking about them.

00:03:35.958 --> 00:03:38.000
But let's just stay cool, okay? Later.

00:03:45.166 --> 00:03:48.207
{\an8}Dante! Dante! Dante! Dante!

00:03:48.208 --> 00:03:50.791
{\an8}What on earth is going on there?

00:04:04.791 --> 00:04:07.415
- What was the question?
- Were you partying last night?

00:04:07.416 --> 00:04:11.041
Pictures of you at Afterlife are
making the rounds on social media.

00:04:12.625 --> 00:04:15.958
Impossible.
Cameras aren't allowed in there.

00:04:17.583 --> 00:04:19.832
You think your performance is funny, too?

00:04:19.833 --> 00:04:22.457
Your escapades got you kicked out
of Formula 1.

00:04:22.458 --> 00:04:24.290
- WHAT'S THE PLAN?
- I'M GONNA END THIS!

00:04:24.291 --> 00:04:27.082
You're in third place
after five Euro GT races.

00:04:27.083 --> 00:04:28.124
Last year, Ruben,

00:04:28.125 --> 00:04:31.624
who had been benched because of you,
came in first place.

00:04:31.625 --> 00:04:35.415
The Lamont race is next week, but
you're partying and letting yourself go.

00:04:35.416 --> 00:04:38.040
- You've done your research, huh?
- Nothing but the facts.

00:04:38.041 --> 00:04:42.082
The fact is that within the team
we may have different ideas about "how,"

00:04:42.083 --> 00:04:43.332
but not about "what."

00:04:43.333 --> 00:04:46.290
- And what is this "what"?
- Winning the season, what else?

00:04:46.291 --> 00:04:48.040
And what if Dante doesn't win?

00:04:48.041 --> 00:04:52.041
As the team leader, aren't you already
taking a big risk, given his problems?

00:04:56.166 --> 00:04:57.999
We have confidence in Dante.

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:01.707
That's it. Thanks a lot, that's all.
Have a great day, see you next time.

00:05:01.708 --> 00:05:03.041
Dante, one last question.

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:06.665
It's been nearly two years
since your sister's tragic accident.

00:05:06.666 --> 00:05:08.665
Would she be proud of your lifestyle?

00:05:08.666 --> 00:05:11.165
- What did you just say?
- Honestly.

00:05:11.166 --> 00:05:12.540
- Okay.
- You son of a bitch!

00:05:12.541 --> 00:05:13.707
- Hey!
- That's too much!

00:05:13.708 --> 00:05:15.165
- Stop!
- Get out!

00:05:15.166 --> 00:05:16.291
- What did you say?
- Hey!

00:05:17.125 --> 00:05:18.332
Hey!

00:05:18.333 --> 00:05:20.874
No alcohol, no parties, no nothing!

00:05:20.875 --> 00:05:22.915
It's all in the contract,
in black and white.

00:05:22.916 --> 00:05:25.582
Last night's pictures mean
a 20,000 euro fine!

00:05:25.583 --> 00:05:27.707
And that stunt in there? Another 20.

00:05:27.708 --> 00:05:30.540
- I know my contract.
- Then act like it.

00:05:30.541 --> 00:05:31.625
Okay, that's enough.

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:35.791
Dante, you good?

00:05:36.333 --> 00:05:38.750
Or do you want Ruben
to take over the training?

00:05:39.750 --> 00:05:40.583
Dream on.

00:05:41.166 --> 00:05:43.208
Go, get outta here, you three. Go train.

00:05:44.333 --> 00:05:45.375
Come on, let's go.

00:06:07.583 --> 00:06:09.707
289 kilometers per hour!

00:06:09.708 --> 00:06:12.625
Maybe we should
set reporters on you more often, kid.

00:06:25.083 --> 00:06:26.750
That's a record!

00:06:27.166 --> 00:06:28.749
- Sweet!
- Yes!

00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:31.833
I get that you're angry, Mr. Richter.
I am, too.

00:06:34.708 --> 00:06:35.791
I understand.

00:06:41.916 --> 00:06:42.832
And?

00:06:42.833 --> 00:06:45.833
Our biggest sponsor is pulling out
until further notice.

00:06:52.208 --> 00:06:53.916
Get ready for the pit stop.

00:06:55.166 --> 00:06:57.875
- You ready, Sarah?
- Yeah, I'm ready.

00:07:05.833 --> 00:07:08.999
No way! Hey, Timo! Is this for real?

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:11.708
- Man, bunch of amateurs here.
- Wait, I have a spare part.

00:07:17.416 --> 00:07:20.582
Okay, folks.
Nearly perfect doesn't win races.

00:07:20.583 --> 00:07:24.166
It would have been a great time
had Timo not screwed up again. Thanks.

00:07:27.041 --> 00:07:29.832
You can thank the newbie.

00:07:29.833 --> 00:07:32.750
This is Sarah.
She's the new mechanic on the team.

00:07:33.250 --> 00:07:35.624
- All right. So, from now on, total focus…
- Thanks.

00:07:35.625 --> 00:07:37.125
…on the Lamont race!

00:07:37.708 --> 00:07:39.750
Your friends and families have been told!

00:07:40.291 --> 00:07:42.208
They won't be seeing you before Christmas.

00:07:55.916 --> 00:07:57.000
Sarah?

00:07:58.333 --> 00:07:59.499
Hey.

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:00.458
Awesome.

00:08:01.208 --> 00:08:04.041
- It's been a long time.
- Yeah. Hey.

00:08:05.291 --> 00:08:08.458
Yeah, Kids' Kart Racing, 2012.

00:08:10.333 --> 00:08:12.708
- "See you at the finish line!"
- Yeah.

00:08:13.458 --> 00:08:15.541
Weren't you even faster than me one time?

00:08:16.375 --> 00:08:19.790
- One time?
- Well, we'll see about that.

00:08:19.791 --> 00:08:21.750
So, how are you? Still driving?

00:08:23.083 --> 00:08:25.416
Only on the PlayStation.

00:08:26.583 --> 00:08:27.666
That makes two of us.

00:08:29.541 --> 00:08:31.499
Why didn't you say anything?

00:08:31.500 --> 00:08:33.583
I could've put in a good word for you.

00:08:35.041 --> 00:08:36.583
I wanted to do it by myself.

00:08:40.166 --> 00:08:41.166
Makes sense.

00:08:45.791 --> 00:08:46.875
How's your mom?

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:52.083
Good.

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:55.833
Good.

00:08:58.083 --> 00:08:59.083
Can you…

00:09:00.166 --> 00:09:01.957
Give her my best regards.

00:09:01.958 --> 00:09:04.375
Yeah, I will. See you.

00:09:05.708 --> 00:09:09.041
And… if you ever need someone to talk to…

00:09:10.416 --> 00:09:11.500
Any time.

00:10:11.083 --> 00:10:12.790
- You're Sarah, right?
- Yes.

00:10:12.791 --> 00:10:15.583
I'm Tanya. I do press and marketing.

00:10:16.583 --> 00:10:18.208
- Nice to meet you.
- Nice to meet you.

00:10:21.375 --> 00:10:22.499
Oh, no, not her.

00:10:22.500 --> 00:10:24.040
EVA MARIA FISCHER
CELEBRITY EXPERT

00:10:24.041 --> 00:10:25.083
Oh, God.

00:10:26.833 --> 00:10:27.999
Note for tomorrow.

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:31.875
Call Eva Maria Fischer's editors.

00:10:33.583 --> 00:10:35.291
Here's a little tip, by the way.

00:10:36.208 --> 00:10:39.499
Anyone who wants to get along with Dante,

00:10:39.500 --> 00:10:42.624
never talk to him about his sister.

00:10:42.625 --> 00:10:44.083
Never, ever.

00:10:44.833 --> 00:10:45.666
Yeah.

00:11:12.791 --> 00:11:14.041
This room's for everyone.

00:11:15.333 --> 00:11:16.833
You don't mind?

00:11:17.916 --> 00:11:18.750
No.

00:11:20.166 --> 00:11:21.250
It'd be weird anyway.

00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:24.541
You're part of the team, after all.

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:36.083
Shit.

00:11:41.041 --> 00:11:43.583
- Hold still.
- You got any scissors or something?

00:11:46.625 --> 00:11:47.458
Hold still.

00:11:51.333 --> 00:11:53.166
If you want to work for me,

00:11:54.875 --> 00:11:56.541
we have to trust each other blindly.

00:12:01.958 --> 00:12:02.791
Okay?

00:12:03.708 --> 00:12:04.750
Okay.

00:12:08.958 --> 00:12:10.833
If you ever need help,

00:12:12.583 --> 00:12:14.250
just let me know.

00:12:19.833 --> 00:12:20.875
See you, Sandra.

00:12:22.083 --> 00:12:23.041
Sarah.

00:12:37.833 --> 00:12:38.875
Mom?

00:13:04.833 --> 00:13:08.875
REGARDING: DEBTS
DEAR MRS. JENKINS,

00:13:25.500 --> 00:13:27.708
KART RACING
1st PLACE

00:13:45.333 --> 00:13:48.375
I want to be a driver, too. Like you.

00:13:48.916 --> 00:13:51.041
{\an8}Once a driver, always a driver.

00:13:56.208 --> 00:13:58.665
{\an8}ESCALATED PRESS CONFERENCE
TEAM EAGLE

00:13:58.666 --> 00:14:01.000
- What did you say?
- Get out!

00:14:16.041 --> 00:14:18.457
How's Dante Annunziata doing?

00:14:18.458 --> 00:14:21.915
Not good, I tell you what. First,
the crazy stories about his affairs,

00:14:21.916 --> 00:14:24.749
and then the excessive drinking
and endless parties.

00:14:24.750 --> 00:14:27.874
No wonder he was
kicked out of Formula 1 last year.

00:14:27.875 --> 00:14:30.499
Since the death of his sister,
he seems totally lost.

00:14:30.500 --> 00:14:33.750
{\an8}It's a shame when you remember
that he was right at the top.

00:14:45.958 --> 00:14:49.207
{\an8}Oh, my God, guys.
Have you seen this photo?

00:14:49.208 --> 00:14:52.540
{\an8}I'm so totally shocked.
What's going on with Dante Annunziata?

00:14:52.541 --> 00:14:53.666
I don't know who…

00:14:58.375 --> 00:14:59.791
{\an8}WHAT HAPPENED
IN THE LOCKER ROOM?

00:15:03.958 --> 00:15:05.207
Whoa! Dante!

00:15:05.208 --> 00:15:06.791
I want to know all the details.

00:15:08.791 --> 00:15:13.290
{\an8}The racing star and the mechanic.
A steamy workplace romance.

00:15:13.291 --> 00:15:15.333
{\an8}The sponsors are not happy at all.

00:15:18.750 --> 00:15:20.083
- What?
- Fuck!

00:15:21.916 --> 00:15:23.708
I swear, nothing happened.
It was nothing.

00:15:26.541 --> 00:15:27.665
Sarah.

00:15:27.666 --> 00:15:28.750
Not now, okay?

00:15:30.166 --> 00:15:33.124
This is a huge media scandal.
The sponsors are going nuts.

00:15:33.125 --> 00:15:35.540
- You are suspended.
- It's a misunderstanding.

00:15:35.541 --> 00:15:39.250
- I can explain. I don't know how…
- It is what it is.

00:15:40.708 --> 00:15:43.707
- I have to let you go.
- But nothing happened!

00:15:43.708 --> 00:15:45.166
I'm sorry.

00:15:57.958 --> 00:16:01.083
Richter will pull out as a sponsor
if you continue to race with us.

00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:06.665
You're not just our driver, Dante.

00:16:06.666 --> 00:16:09.832
You're our face, too. A brand ambassador!

00:16:09.833 --> 00:16:14.333
And right now, you are
an absolute disaster for the brand.

00:16:23.458 --> 00:16:25.083
You're not a good role model.

00:16:26.291 --> 00:16:28.416
I never was.

00:16:40.458 --> 00:16:41.833
Well, you're right.

00:16:42.666 --> 00:16:45.083
It's true.
For us, it's not just about winning.

00:16:46.375 --> 00:16:47.625
We need a story.

00:16:48.583 --> 00:16:50.750
We need to tell people a story.

00:16:51.791 --> 00:16:53.333
What kind of story?

00:17:18.208 --> 00:17:19.250
Sarah?

00:17:27.750 --> 00:17:29.250
Are you lost?

00:17:30.666 --> 00:17:31.500
No.

00:17:41.416 --> 00:17:44.291
I think we have both had
a pretty shitty day.

00:17:46.666 --> 00:17:48.125
I'm unemployed.

00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:53.000
You've got 600 horsepower under that hood.
Your day can't be that shitty.

00:17:55.375 --> 00:17:58.625
Okay. Snappy, like your father.

00:18:01.916 --> 00:18:04.833
I knew him.
From back when he was still racing.

00:18:05.541 --> 00:18:06.583
A huge talent.

00:18:09.250 --> 00:18:11.750
But without money,
you can't go far in this sport.

00:18:14.458 --> 00:18:17.207
I know how much Tommy believed in you.

00:18:17.208 --> 00:18:20.916
That he went into debt
financing your dream.

00:18:24.458 --> 00:18:28.041
My father wasn't cold in the ground
before a letter came from the tax office.

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:30.375
180,000 euros.

00:18:31.583 --> 00:18:34.250
That's been hanging over us
ever since I was 16.

00:18:35.041 --> 00:18:36.500
You feel responsible.

00:18:39.833 --> 00:18:41.125
Why are you here?

00:18:46.750 --> 00:18:47.583
Test drive.

00:19:06.375 --> 00:19:08.958
You've got 600 horsepower under the hood.

00:19:10.208 --> 00:19:11.999
Not such a shitty day anymore, is it?

00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:16.374
If this is about me going public,
don't worry, that's not who I am.

00:19:16.375 --> 00:19:18.666
- No, that's not it.
- So what is this about?

00:19:19.333 --> 00:19:21.750
A deal that's good for everyone.

00:19:30.208 --> 00:19:33.208
In public, you play Dante's sweetheart
until the end of the season.

00:19:34.375 --> 00:19:35.916
And in return…

00:19:37.250 --> 00:19:40.625
Sarah, wait. Sarah, wait a minute.

00:19:42.000 --> 00:19:43.583
I'll pay off your debt.

00:19:44.208 --> 00:19:46.875
All of it. The whole 180,000.

00:19:49.208 --> 00:19:50.416
And that's not all.

00:19:51.250 --> 00:19:52.750
You want to drive.

00:19:54.583 --> 00:19:56.166
I mean, really drive.

00:19:57.791 --> 00:20:00.207
I'm giving you the chance
to be the first woman driver

00:20:00.208 --> 00:20:02.166
in the history of Eagle Racing.

00:20:03.625 --> 00:20:06.540
If Dante wins the season,
he's back in Formula 1.

00:20:06.541 --> 00:20:09.500
If he loses, he's out.
Either way, I need a new number one.

00:20:10.958 --> 00:20:12.875
Ruben? What about Ruben?

00:20:13.500 --> 00:20:15.041
Not if you're faster.

00:20:16.708 --> 00:20:19.624
I see what your father saw in you, Sarah.

00:20:19.625 --> 00:20:21.582
And I'm ready to invest.

00:20:21.583 --> 00:20:25.624
Play the role of Dante's girlfriend,
and put this scandal to bed,

00:20:25.625 --> 00:20:29.166
and I'll get you the best training
money can buy.

00:20:31.083 --> 00:20:32.750
But there is one condition.

00:20:34.208 --> 00:20:38.124
No one can know
about our little agreement. No one.

00:20:38.125 --> 00:20:39.749
Certainly not Dante.

00:20:39.750 --> 00:20:42.624
He must not know about your training.

00:20:42.625 --> 00:20:44.958
He thinks this is his story.

00:20:47.041 --> 00:20:48.125
Make it yours.

00:20:49.375 --> 00:20:50.208
You hear me?

00:20:50.958 --> 00:20:52.083
Make it yours.

00:21:03.375 --> 00:21:06.124
"In return for this undertaking,
Eagle Racing agrees,

00:21:06.125 --> 00:21:08.749
upon fulfilment,
to provide the following."

00:21:08.750 --> 00:21:12.540
"First, a payment of 200,000 euros
to Ms. Jenkins."

00:21:12.541 --> 00:21:13.874
As if that's believable.

00:21:13.875 --> 00:21:16.874
People will talk about it,
and that's what matters.

00:21:16.875 --> 00:21:18.541
Manipulate, confuse and destroy.

00:21:19.875 --> 00:21:24.499
"Second, both parties agree
to make their social media

00:21:24.500 --> 00:21:28.125
and other media appearances
fully available, and

00:21:29.833 --> 00:21:33.416
to display affection in public
as circumstances require."

00:21:34.041 --> 00:21:34.916
What?

00:21:36.375 --> 00:21:39.082
Holding hands, shopping arm in arm,
that kind of thing.

00:21:39.083 --> 00:21:41.666
Kissing.
We're talking about kissing, okay?

00:21:42.625 --> 00:21:44.375
Do we know if she's healthy?

00:21:46.208 --> 00:21:47.833
Sorry, who are you?

00:21:49.666 --> 00:21:50.875
His mother.

00:21:51.833 --> 00:21:54.624
Dante can't catch anything
during the season.

00:21:54.625 --> 00:21:57.832
The guy who never sleeps
with the same woman twice?

00:21:57.833 --> 00:21:58.666
Says who?

00:21:59.458 --> 00:22:00.582
The Internet.

00:22:00.583 --> 00:22:03.249
Tomorrow, the Internet will say
that I love you.

00:22:03.250 --> 00:22:04.250
Go on, please.

00:22:05.541 --> 00:22:09.707
"Emphasized here in particular as
an explicit stipulation of the contract,

00:22:09.708 --> 00:22:14.083
a kiss on the red carpet
at the European Sports Awards in Monaco."

00:22:15.041 --> 00:22:18.457
"This contract is strictly confidential."

00:22:18.458 --> 00:22:21.499
It doesn't say that
there are no other verbal agreements.

00:22:21.500 --> 00:22:23.333
Normally, that's standard, isn't it?

00:22:25.208 --> 00:22:27.290
No problem. Consider it agreed.

00:22:27.291 --> 00:22:28.208
Good.

00:22:44.666 --> 00:22:47.416
You don't touch me without my permission.

00:22:47.916 --> 00:22:49.500
It'll be my pleasure.

00:22:53.541 --> 00:22:55.624
Where did we meet?

00:22:55.625 --> 00:22:56.624
Good question!

00:22:56.625 --> 00:23:01.624
It wasn't just love at first sight,
but a savior in a moment of need.

00:23:01.625 --> 00:23:05.540
An eye-wateringly expensive restaurant
high above the city skyline.

00:23:05.541 --> 00:23:07.916
You saw her and reacted at once.

00:23:08.750 --> 00:23:09.708
Are you all right?

00:23:10.708 --> 00:23:13.750
- Isn't that a bit much?
- So she should have choked?

00:23:16.791 --> 00:23:19.124
- Of course not.
- So, anyway…

00:23:19.125 --> 00:23:23.790
In that moment, there was a spark.
Love at first sight.

00:23:23.791 --> 00:23:24.749
Thank you.

00:23:24.750 --> 00:23:27.541
But it was a false start.
They didn't exchange numbers.

00:23:28.208 --> 00:23:31.957
Tough situation.
But destiny doesn't give up that easily,

00:23:31.958 --> 00:23:34.166
and so it shifted things up a gear.

00:23:34.750 --> 00:23:38.083
It was Sarah's first day at Team Eagle
and whoosh!

00:23:42.208 --> 00:23:45.749
Suddenly, you see each other again,
and the world stands still.

00:23:45.750 --> 00:23:49.290
Meaningful glances, racing pulses,
the works.

00:23:49.291 --> 00:23:51.374
Just like in the movies.

00:23:51.375 --> 00:23:53.583
From then on, you really hit the gas.

00:23:54.916 --> 00:23:57.916
Love in the fast lane,
and in pole position.

00:23:58.625 --> 00:24:00.665
And today is the big day.

00:24:00.666 --> 00:24:04.999
The day that a video of you
going shopping for rings will go viral.

00:24:05.000 --> 00:24:09.457
Not just any ring.
White gold, 15 karat, at least.

00:24:09.458 --> 00:24:12.124
Sarah has no idea, of course,

00:24:12.125 --> 00:24:15.707
as she heads back to the place
where it all began.

00:24:15.708 --> 00:24:16.625
That's good.

00:24:18.375 --> 00:24:19.250
Yeah.

00:24:36.500 --> 00:24:37.625
You're drooling.

00:24:42.250 --> 00:24:43.624
I can't do this.

00:24:43.625 --> 00:24:46.041
I imagine that women hear that
from you pretty often.

00:24:47.750 --> 00:24:50.125
Pretty dry.
I bet there's sand in your gearbox.

00:24:53.666 --> 00:24:56.083
Thanks. I needed that.

00:25:02.750 --> 00:25:03.791
What are you doing?

00:25:04.500 --> 00:25:06.291
Making the biggest mistake of my life.

00:25:10.000 --> 00:25:12.125
Will you marry me?

00:25:14.791 --> 00:25:15.750
Of course.

00:25:21.750 --> 00:25:24.708
- Did you pick it out all by yourself?
- Shut up.

00:25:25.541 --> 00:25:29.249
It now turns out that racing driver
Dante Annunziata

00:25:29.250 --> 00:25:33.624
{\an8}is driving in the fast lane,
heading for pole position.

00:25:33.625 --> 00:25:38.165
From major scandal to great love.

00:25:38.166 --> 00:25:41.583
- You're a PR genius.
- Oh, God. Eva Maria Fischer, thank you.

00:25:42.625 --> 00:25:43.874
Oh, God.

00:25:43.875 --> 00:25:47.915
I understand that you're overwhelmed.
I am, too, but…

00:25:47.916 --> 00:25:50.499
It's not what everyone thinks. He's…

00:25:50.500 --> 00:25:53.999
He's charming and funny, and…

00:25:54.000 --> 00:25:56.457
He has such beautiful eyes.

00:25:56.458 --> 00:26:01.041
He smells really good. He's a catch.

00:26:04.333 --> 00:26:05.583
Look at me.

00:26:06.416 --> 00:26:08.041
Something's not right here.

00:26:08.625 --> 00:26:11.332
You've never even mentioned this guy.

00:26:11.333 --> 00:26:13.833
And all of sudden, you're engaged?

00:26:15.333 --> 00:26:16.916
And you're flying to Monaco?

00:26:19.750 --> 00:26:21.500
You're hiding something from me.

00:26:25.750 --> 00:26:27.541
Promise me you'll keep this a secret?

00:26:29.375 --> 00:26:30.291
Okay.

00:26:31.500 --> 00:26:34.333
Our debts are about
to go away forever. Here.

00:26:36.625 --> 00:26:37.750
{\an8}In black and white.

00:26:38.458 --> 00:26:40.874
{\an8}Mom, they're paying us 200,000 euros.

00:26:40.875 --> 00:26:45.333
{\an8}And all I have to do is
pretend to be engaged to an idiot.

00:26:48.625 --> 00:26:50.083
- Sweetie…
- Mom, please.

00:26:51.541 --> 00:26:53.041
I can do this.

00:27:24.166 --> 00:27:26.749
So, little update on tonight's gala.

00:27:26.750 --> 00:27:28.499
Pickup is at 8:00 p.m.

00:27:28.500 --> 00:27:29.832
On the dot. Downstairs.

00:27:29.833 --> 00:27:35.124
The makeup artist figures you'll be done
in two-and-a-half, three hours.

00:27:35.125 --> 00:27:36.124
Three hours?

00:27:36.125 --> 00:27:37.625
- Yeah.
- If that's all it takes.

00:27:38.875 --> 00:27:40.124
That's mean.

00:27:40.125 --> 00:27:42.957
So, don't worry about a thing.

00:27:42.958 --> 00:27:45.666
I know you're gonna look amazing. Okay?

00:27:46.208 --> 00:27:49.790
And in terms of styling,
you've got a few options ready, right?

00:27:49.791 --> 00:27:51.082
You mean clothes?

00:27:51.083 --> 00:27:53.832
I mean evening gowns. So, yes, clothes.

00:27:53.833 --> 00:27:57.582
This was all in the email
that I expect you've read.

00:27:57.583 --> 00:27:59.707
Yes. Yes.

00:27:59.708 --> 00:28:03.790
Perfect, my fiancée is walking
down the red carpet in gym clothes.

00:28:03.791 --> 00:28:07.249
Better than your models
in their see-through outfits!

00:28:07.250 --> 00:28:08.791
They have nothing to hide, is all.

00:28:10.208 --> 00:28:12.375
Is that why you're not wearing
see-through pants?

00:28:14.750 --> 00:28:15.583
Touché.

00:28:41.750 --> 00:28:44.665
Welcome back, Signore Annunziata.

00:28:44.666 --> 00:28:46.957
It's always a pleasure to see you.

00:28:46.958 --> 00:28:49.040
The pleasure is all mine.

00:28:49.041 --> 00:28:51.541
The same room as last time?

00:28:55.833 --> 00:28:59.958
Oh, the honeymoon suite
has been booked for you.

00:29:02.958 --> 00:29:08.207
That's what it says in the system.
For Mr. Annunziata and Ms. Jenkins.

00:29:08.208 --> 00:29:11.707
- Jenkins.
- Ms. Jenkins.

00:29:11.708 --> 00:29:12.708
Jenkins.

00:29:14.958 --> 00:29:17.833
This is all a little new for both of us.

00:29:18.500 --> 00:29:19.458
Right.

00:29:20.041 --> 00:29:20.875
Come along.

00:29:26.833 --> 00:29:30.457
Fuck whoever you want,
but you're getting your own room.

00:29:30.458 --> 00:29:32.500
- You jealous?
- No.

00:29:33.083 --> 00:29:36.000
Just struck by how consistent you are
about trophy hunting.

00:29:36.916 --> 00:29:39.500
Unlike you, I get paid for it.

00:29:42.875 --> 00:29:45.374
I hear you used to race, too?

00:29:45.375 --> 00:29:47.541
German Junior Kart Champion 2014.

00:29:48.166 --> 00:29:49.833
Once a driver, always a driver.

00:29:50.500 --> 00:29:52.750
That's what people
who aren't drivers anymore say.

00:29:53.708 --> 00:29:55.041
If you say so.

00:30:17.250 --> 00:30:20.290
You take the bedroom.
I'll take the couch. No problem.

00:30:20.291 --> 00:30:21.375
Strawberry?

00:30:27.791 --> 00:30:29.290
I only like white chocolate.

00:30:29.291 --> 00:30:31.207
- That's not chocolate.
- Question of taste.

00:30:31.208 --> 00:30:32.333
Question of character.

00:30:34.500 --> 00:30:36.958
I'm just not the bitter type.

00:30:45.958 --> 00:30:50.165
Hi, it's Tanya again. Send me
a couple of outfit options for tonight.

00:30:50.166 --> 00:30:51.749
- Thanks, kiss kiss.
- Shit.

00:30:51.750 --> 00:30:52.832
When's your flight?

00:30:52.833 --> 00:30:54.665
Mom, we arrived today.

00:30:54.666 --> 00:30:56.082
- Not tomorrow?
- No.

00:30:56.083 --> 00:30:57.500
Then I can't come with you.

00:31:18.625 --> 00:31:19.666
Hello?

00:31:36.916 --> 00:31:38.333
Can I help you?

00:31:40.166 --> 00:31:41.750
I think I'm in the wrong place.

00:31:43.541 --> 00:31:46.124
Sarah… Sarah Jenkins!

00:31:46.125 --> 00:31:47.958
You're in the right place. Welcome.

00:31:48.791 --> 00:31:50.082
How do you know me?

00:31:50.083 --> 00:31:53.874
Everyone knows
Dante Annunziata's fiancée. Hello?

00:31:53.875 --> 00:31:55.957
He has a really good eye.

00:31:55.958 --> 00:31:59.249
Being honest?
When I saw you from behind, I thought,

00:31:59.250 --> 00:32:01.249
"Security! Get this hobo outta here!"

00:32:01.250 --> 00:32:03.332
But, my God, you're pretty. Unbelievable!

00:32:03.333 --> 00:32:05.625
Looking for something
for the awards show tonight?

00:32:07.583 --> 00:32:08.458
Yes.

00:32:11.541 --> 00:32:13.375
Okay, this could work, right?

00:32:13.958 --> 00:32:15.290
No, too big.

00:32:15.291 --> 00:32:18.207
You could wear this as a parachute,
but not to the gala.

00:32:18.208 --> 00:32:19.416
We'll find something.

00:32:21.583 --> 00:32:23.874
You look a little bit like E.T.

00:32:23.875 --> 00:32:26.582
- Like a ball bearing.
- Or a conspiracy theorist.

00:32:26.583 --> 00:32:28.707
I like the yellow one.

00:32:28.708 --> 00:32:30.125
No, that's too… too basic.

00:32:32.166 --> 00:32:34.291
Oh, that's also really, really nice.

00:32:56.041 --> 00:32:58.041
I think it's… too much.

00:32:58.791 --> 00:32:59.958
It's beautiful.

00:33:00.708 --> 00:33:02.291
I prefer the black one.

00:33:03.041 --> 00:33:04.541
That one's beautiful too.

00:33:11.083 --> 00:33:14.291
- So, that'll be…
- Perfect timing!

00:33:17.416 --> 00:33:19.416
Guess you didn't have anything on you?

00:33:20.875 --> 00:33:24.707
That will be 6,600 euros.

00:33:24.708 --> 00:33:27.582
- What?
- And the sparkly dress too, please.

00:33:27.583 --> 00:33:28.416
Okay.

00:33:36.583 --> 00:33:37.750
You were watching me.

00:33:39.791 --> 00:33:41.250
You like the thought of that?

00:33:49.208 --> 00:33:51.250
Your makeup artist is waiting for you.

00:34:54.666 --> 00:34:55.500
Hey.

00:35:00.250 --> 00:35:01.957
Do I look halfway decent?

00:35:01.958 --> 00:35:06.333
"Halfway decent" would be
the understatement of the year.

00:35:09.125 --> 00:35:10.999
It only took three hours, after all.

00:35:11.000 --> 00:35:13.416
I can't leave you alone for a moment.

00:35:16.166 --> 00:35:17.708
And how could I?

00:35:22.458 --> 00:35:24.958
Hey, spare. How was your flight?

00:35:27.083 --> 00:35:28.750
Not great, I gotta say.

00:35:29.333 --> 00:35:31.082
Like your sense of humor.

00:35:31.083 --> 00:35:32.915
Hey, hey. There you are!

00:35:32.916 --> 00:35:37.333
Wow, you three look great.
Time to get going. The shuttle's here.

00:35:50.541 --> 00:35:51.708
You two ever have a thing?

00:35:53.708 --> 00:35:54.833
Who?

00:35:57.250 --> 00:35:58.083
You and Ruben?

00:35:58.750 --> 00:35:59.874
No.

00:35:59.875 --> 00:36:02.375
We were in the same karting school.

00:36:06.875 --> 00:36:08.166
Jealous?

00:36:09.958 --> 00:36:11.125
It's just a job.

00:36:12.791 --> 00:36:14.250
No more, no less.

00:36:59.083 --> 00:37:00.083
Everything okay?

00:37:05.833 --> 00:37:06.833
Kiss!

00:37:08.041 --> 00:37:09.915
- Look at the camera.
- This way, everyone!

00:37:09.916 --> 00:37:10.958
Can you kiss now?

00:37:12.666 --> 00:37:14.583
It's just a job, right?

00:37:17.458 --> 00:37:18.541
It's all fake.

00:37:19.250 --> 00:37:20.375
It's all fake.

00:38:12.791 --> 00:38:16.040
And welcome to this year's
European Sports Awards,

00:38:16.041 --> 00:38:17.082
live from Monaco.

00:38:17.083 --> 00:38:20.124
My name is Steven Gätjen,
and this is the first highlight

00:38:20.125 --> 00:38:21.915
from today's awards ceremony.

00:38:21.916 --> 00:38:23.540
Here's Dante Annunziata.

00:38:23.541 --> 00:38:27.165
No trophy this time,
but with Sarah and a kiss

00:38:27.166 --> 00:38:30.499
that will have hearts racing
on the red carpet.

00:38:30.500 --> 00:38:32.583
That is true love.

00:38:48.000 --> 00:38:50.875
- Mr. Richter!
- Here they come.

00:38:51.416 --> 00:38:52.583
Our dream couple.

00:38:55.583 --> 00:38:58.665
Even better looking in the flesh
than in pictures.

00:38:58.666 --> 00:39:01.082
- It's a pleasure to meet you.
- Likewise.

00:39:01.083 --> 00:39:03.749
It's great that he was able
to score you so quickly,

00:39:03.750 --> 00:39:06.416
but I'd prefer a win at Lamont.

00:39:08.041 --> 00:39:09.208
We're working on it.

00:39:10.041 --> 00:39:14.416
I see from the papers
that you've put his little fire out?

00:39:15.041 --> 00:39:15.958
Have I?

00:39:16.958 --> 00:39:20.500
Sarah has helped me discover
a new side of myself.

00:39:21.458 --> 00:39:23.333
The main thing is to not get any slower.

00:39:28.458 --> 00:39:31.124
You bear a striking resemblance
to your sister.

00:39:31.125 --> 00:39:33.458
You really are her spitting image.

00:39:35.833 --> 00:39:37.000
Did you know Gabriella?

00:39:38.833 --> 00:39:40.582
Personally? No.

00:39:40.583 --> 00:39:46.333
But I understand
she was a very talented driver.

00:39:47.625 --> 00:39:50.041
Excuse me. Come along, I want to dance.

00:39:51.416 --> 00:39:52.250
Thank you.

00:39:54.291 --> 00:39:55.624
What an asshole.

00:39:55.625 --> 00:39:58.582
How dare he provoke you like that!

00:39:58.583 --> 00:39:59.583
Hey.

00:40:00.791 --> 00:40:03.125
You look really beautiful in that dress.

00:40:05.541 --> 00:40:07.916
And it's not even see-through.

00:40:16.416 --> 00:40:18.000
Did you wear it for me?

00:40:21.125 --> 00:40:22.458
Maybe.

00:40:27.500 --> 00:40:30.208
But don't expect me
to take it off for you.

00:40:37.541 --> 00:40:39.750
Aren't they sweet?

00:40:41.166 --> 00:40:43.041
Almost too good to be true.

00:40:43.750 --> 00:40:46.125
Some people are saying
that it's all a hoax.

00:40:49.583 --> 00:40:50.416
Who?

00:40:52.625 --> 00:40:55.665
…who took pictures
of Dante and Sarah shopping.

00:40:55.666 --> 00:40:59.625
It doesn't look like they're in love.
Is this all fake?

00:41:01.791 --> 00:41:05.875
I think that looks pretty authentic,
if you ask my opinion.

00:41:37.750 --> 00:41:40.083
You can stop, no one can see us here.

00:41:40.666 --> 00:41:42.125
What if I don't want to?

00:42:33.541 --> 00:42:34.666
Good morning. Sleep well?

00:42:35.625 --> 00:42:38.249
- Yes.
- Your kiss yesterday, that was…

00:42:38.250 --> 00:42:42.375
It was a convincing performance.
Excellent work. Check, please.

00:42:44.375 --> 00:42:45.375
You're welcome.

00:42:45.916 --> 00:42:49.541
So, our deal stands.
Training starts after Lamont.

00:42:53.541 --> 00:42:55.541
- Are you still there?
- Yeah, yeah.

00:42:57.041 --> 00:42:58.915
I'm still here. I…

00:42:58.916 --> 00:43:02.541
- I'm looking forward to it.
- Remember, not a word to Dante.

00:43:28.041 --> 00:43:32.375
I think I'm clearly the cuter of us two.

00:43:38.250 --> 00:43:41.833
Interesting experience,
to be the one waking up alone.

00:43:48.208 --> 00:43:50.416
There's a first time for everything.

00:43:57.833 --> 00:44:02.875
Do you want to tell me
that last night was a mistake?

00:44:04.500 --> 00:44:08.083
That everything should stay
strictly business between us?

00:44:12.666 --> 00:44:14.250
Exactly.

00:44:16.000 --> 00:44:17.166
I'm sorry.

00:44:32.375 --> 00:44:37.208
The Grand Prix of Lamont, with its
traditionally unpredictable weather.

00:44:38.875 --> 00:44:41.415
Here and now,
absolutely anything could happen.

00:44:41.416 --> 00:44:43.750
It's an important date
in the Euro Masters calendar.

00:44:46.291 --> 00:44:48.290
Tough conditions again today.

00:44:48.291 --> 00:44:51.332
The fans have a really exciting race
to look forward to,

00:44:51.333 --> 00:44:54.125
but for the teams,
this will be a test of their courage.

00:45:15.166 --> 00:45:17.500
It won't be an easy day for him.

00:45:19.041 --> 00:45:20.250
Why not?

00:45:22.083 --> 00:45:24.083
It's his sister's birthday.

00:45:26.375 --> 00:45:28.541
Today of all days.

00:45:35.541 --> 00:45:38.000
Hey, take care of yourself, Sarah.

00:45:39.500 --> 00:45:40.582
What do you mean?

00:45:40.583 --> 00:45:44.375
What do I mean?
I can see you have feelings for him.

00:45:47.250 --> 00:45:48.083
Nonsense!

00:45:49.375 --> 00:45:51.665
Bronson told me about your little deal.

00:45:51.666 --> 00:45:54.583
You've got big plans. Don't forget that.

00:46:02.000 --> 00:46:04.249
And now it's almost time.

00:46:04.250 --> 00:46:08.374
A few seconds from the start.
The Grand Prix of Lamont.

00:46:08.375 --> 00:46:11.582
Annunziata is starting in fifth place,
after a tough qualifying session,

00:46:11.583 --> 00:46:16.707
and he'll need a minor miracle today
if he wants a shot at the championship.

00:46:16.708 --> 00:46:19.208
Second place, at least. No easy task.

00:46:23.625 --> 00:46:24.958
Come on.

00:46:38.666 --> 00:46:41.790
Very good start from Annunziata,
off to a flying start in this race.

00:46:41.791 --> 00:46:43.083
Good performance.

00:46:46.125 --> 00:46:49.540
Annunziata is in top form,
masterfully overtaking McKinnen here.

00:46:49.541 --> 00:46:51.916
In third place now. Who saw this coming?

00:46:52.916 --> 00:46:56.875
Ninth lap. The three drivers
around Annunziata are neck-and-neck.

00:46:59.583 --> 00:47:03.374
This kind of supremacy on the racetrack
is the reason he was signed.

00:47:03.375 --> 00:47:06.208
Dante Annunziata
is really delivering today.

00:47:07.375 --> 00:47:11.749
And there it is, Annunziata takes the lead
on the 16th lap, against all odds.

00:47:11.750 --> 00:47:12.790
Unbelievable.

00:47:12.791 --> 00:47:13.750
Yes!

00:47:25.875 --> 00:47:28.957
I've got…
I've got a problem with the gear shift.

00:47:28.958 --> 00:47:30.666
Okay.

00:47:31.833 --> 00:47:33.374
Everything looks good on my end.

00:47:33.375 --> 00:47:36.875
Last lap at Lamont.
Will Annunziata close it out today?

00:47:44.875 --> 00:47:46.249
What's he doing?

00:47:46.250 --> 00:47:50.082
No, Annunziata throws away victory,
so close to the finish line.

00:47:50.083 --> 00:47:51.416
Second place.

00:47:52.083 --> 00:47:55.083
His nerves got the better of him.
That's really tough.

00:48:25.375 --> 00:48:26.291
Hey!

00:48:28.291 --> 00:48:31.041
It was a good race. Second place.

00:48:40.833 --> 00:48:44.666
I… I know I shouldn't mention it, but I…

00:48:45.833 --> 00:48:48.208
- I think I know why you…
- Please.

00:48:49.125 --> 00:48:50.999
Spare me the clever advice, okay?

00:48:51.000 --> 00:48:53.540
Believe me, you know nothing about me.

00:48:53.541 --> 00:48:55.915
You don't win races with your head.

00:48:55.916 --> 00:48:57.874
- You win with your heart.
- Your heart?

00:48:57.875 --> 00:49:00.125
Is that your secret to success?

00:49:00.791 --> 00:49:02.583
Junior Kart Champ 2014?

00:49:04.125 --> 00:49:07.332
I'll let you in on a secret.
You're not a driver.

00:49:07.333 --> 00:49:09.875
You never were, and you never will be.

00:49:16.416 --> 00:49:18.583
- Are you okay?
- Leave me alone.

00:49:46.958 --> 00:49:49.208
Don't let anyone tell you what you aren't.

00:50:02.041 --> 00:50:02.958
Promise?

00:50:45.000 --> 00:50:48.040
Sorry, people, but this whole thing
about being fake or not?

00:50:48.041 --> 00:50:50.790
Just look at this fucking kiss!

00:50:50.791 --> 00:50:54.124
Everyone who's ever been
kissed like that knows that it's for real.

00:50:54.125 --> 00:50:55.333
So shut up.

00:50:59.333 --> 00:51:04.750
Sarah Jenkins
hey sorry about

00:51:08.625 --> 00:51:14.875
I'm sorry about

00:51:17.791 --> 00:51:20.583
yo what's up

00:51:27.166 --> 00:51:29.457
Fits like a glove.

00:51:29.458 --> 00:51:31.666
- Can you hear me?
- Loud and clear.

00:51:32.625 --> 00:51:34.000
And are you excited?

00:51:34.875 --> 00:51:35.708
Yes.

00:51:37.791 --> 00:51:38.958
You can do it.

00:51:42.958 --> 00:51:45.708
All right. Let's see if all this secrecy…

00:51:48.625 --> 00:51:50.416
I get it, you can drive.

00:51:53.500 --> 00:51:54.708
Not bad, Sarah.

00:51:56.583 --> 00:52:00.124
- Not bad at all.
- For a woman, you mean?

00:52:00.125 --> 00:52:01.958
No, I'm not like that.

00:52:16.000 --> 00:52:19.750
{\an8}Hey, great training, Sarah.
Keep it up. Pretty impress…

00:52:32.750 --> 00:52:34.125
Hey…

00:52:35.791 --> 00:52:37.833
I shouldn't have said that.

00:52:41.250 --> 00:52:42.416
I'm sorry.

00:52:47.083 --> 00:52:48.000
Good morning.

00:52:49.916 --> 00:52:52.458
So, quick briefing for you two.

00:52:54.958 --> 00:52:59.625
Nothing dramatic. No reason to panic.
But we need to change course.

00:53:00.208 --> 00:53:03.332
Okay, people.
My brother worked in the restaurant

00:53:03.333 --> 00:53:07.290
where Dante Annunziata is supposed
to have saved Sarah's life.

00:53:07.291 --> 00:53:10.540
Strangely, my brother says
that absolutely nobody saw it happen.

00:53:10.541 --> 00:53:11.375
Nobody.

00:53:13.875 --> 00:53:14.999
Yeah.

00:53:15.000 --> 00:53:18.040
It hasn't gotten far yet,
but we need content.

00:53:18.041 --> 00:53:22.124
And good content. So look sharp.

00:53:22.125 --> 00:53:24.583
I've thought of something for tonight.

00:53:25.333 --> 00:53:26.708
Something real.

00:53:28.791 --> 00:53:29.875
I don't believe it.

00:53:30.708 --> 00:53:32.415
Back to the roots.

00:53:32.416 --> 00:53:34.957
- Good idea from Tanya.
- I hear you.

00:53:34.958 --> 00:53:37.457
Yeah, but you don't
stand a chance against me.

00:53:37.458 --> 00:53:39.500
- Oh, yeah?
- I know.

00:53:50.625 --> 00:53:52.625
This is great. It still smells the same.

00:53:54.416 --> 00:53:59.625
Of burnt-out clutch
and adolescent delusions of grandeur.

00:54:04.500 --> 00:54:07.582
Yeah, and of the rancid
snack machine back there.

00:54:07.583 --> 00:54:12.375
We had one of those too,
but it never had gummy bears.

00:54:35.208 --> 00:54:36.208
Is that you?

00:54:37.083 --> 00:54:37.916
Yeah.

00:54:38.958 --> 00:54:40.083
With my dad.

00:54:41.625 --> 00:54:42.625
And who's that?

00:54:44.958 --> 00:54:46.875
- That's Ruben.
- What?

00:54:47.458 --> 00:54:49.750
- What?
- Yeah.

00:54:50.291 --> 00:54:52.958
He was a little huskier back then.

00:54:59.208 --> 00:55:01.750
Your father's eyes are shining.

00:55:03.208 --> 00:55:04.291
Yeah.

00:55:08.541 --> 00:55:10.291
Dad was my hero.

00:55:13.625 --> 00:55:15.416
He always supported me.

00:55:17.041 --> 00:55:19.583
He's the reason
I ever got involved in driving.

00:55:23.166 --> 00:55:25.624
When I was 16, he said,

00:55:25.625 --> 00:55:28.041
"Sarah, no more half measures now."

00:55:29.416 --> 00:55:31.874
And he bought me a brand-new kart.

00:55:31.875 --> 00:55:35.500
With a water-cooled two-stroke engine!
And he found me a real coach.

00:55:37.791 --> 00:55:39.000
The works.

00:55:42.458 --> 00:55:44.666
Six months later, he died.

00:55:46.500 --> 00:55:47.791
Heart attack.

00:55:50.833 --> 00:55:52.415
That was when we found out

00:55:52.416 --> 00:55:55.500
that he'd got himself in debt
so that I could drive.

00:55:57.833 --> 00:55:58.833
I'm sorry.

00:56:06.916 --> 00:56:08.208
You miss her.

00:56:12.208 --> 00:56:13.041
Every day.

00:56:36.416 --> 00:56:39.708
I think Tanya has written us
a different story today.

00:56:58.291 --> 00:57:00.333
- You sabotaged my kart.
- What?

00:57:03.541 --> 00:57:05.833
- You're doping.
- I'm doping?

00:57:06.833 --> 00:57:09.625
I'm so clearly winning there.

00:57:13.208 --> 00:57:14.666
Let's go!

00:57:39.208 --> 00:57:40.999
That was a lot of fun.

00:57:41.000 --> 00:57:43.916
Yeah, I thought so too.

00:57:48.416 --> 00:57:50.500
Do you maybe want to go get a drink?

00:57:53.000 --> 00:57:54.457
Yeah.

00:57:54.458 --> 00:57:57.541
Jack - I'm waiting at the racetrack!
Where are you?

00:58:03.750 --> 00:58:05.416
I gotta go home.

00:58:10.000 --> 00:58:12.874
No problem. Another time.

00:58:12.875 --> 00:58:14.416
Yeah, sorry.

00:58:21.166 --> 00:58:22.707
Sorry, Jack!

00:58:22.708 --> 00:58:24.290
I was with Dante.

00:58:24.291 --> 00:58:25.624
It won't happen again.

00:58:25.625 --> 00:58:28.332
Next time, step on the gas a little more.

00:58:28.333 --> 00:58:29.166
Yeah.

00:58:31.791 --> 00:58:33.291
You can strap yourself in.

00:58:34.250 --> 00:58:35.375
As punishment.

00:58:45.000 --> 00:58:48.624
I want to be a driver, too. Like you.

00:58:48.625 --> 00:58:51.041
Once a driver, always a driver.

00:59:39.708 --> 00:59:42.000
- You just beat the best time.
- What?

00:59:43.000 --> 00:59:44.291
Dante's record.

00:59:47.666 --> 00:59:51.041
That's a new record for the track.
This is incredible, Sarah.

01:00:12.291 --> 01:00:13.833
This woman works so hard.

01:00:15.250 --> 01:00:17.083
- Hey.
- Hey.

01:00:19.833 --> 01:00:22.208
Hey, do you know
if Dante was here last night?

01:00:25.250 --> 01:00:26.790
No idea, why?

01:00:26.791 --> 01:00:29.749
The guys are saying
there's a new record in the system.

01:00:29.750 --> 01:00:30.958
And I didn't do it.

01:00:34.416 --> 01:00:36.416
Could be an error.

01:00:40.833 --> 01:00:41.833
Yeah.

01:00:42.583 --> 01:00:45.541
- I've gotta go shower.
- Okay.

01:00:50.958 --> 01:00:53.957
After a truly stellar
qualifying session yesterday,

01:00:53.958 --> 01:00:57.165
Annunziata could become a nightmare
for the competition

01:00:57.166 --> 01:00:59.958
on the Alpen Racetrack today.

01:01:05.416 --> 01:01:07.124
But of course,

01:01:07.125 --> 01:01:10.124
the winner is just as easy to predict
as the weather around here.

01:01:10.125 --> 01:01:11.374
That is, not at all.

01:01:11.375 --> 01:01:14.333
When it comes to slippery tracks,
McKinnen is the expert.

01:01:20.000 --> 01:01:20.875
Thanks.

01:01:24.708 --> 01:01:25.541
Thank you.

01:01:30.125 --> 01:01:33.166
MOM

01:01:35.583 --> 01:01:36.625
Hey.

01:01:38.000 --> 01:01:38.833
Hi.

01:01:43.041 --> 01:01:45.707
Getting a chance is one thing.

01:01:45.708 --> 01:01:49.040
But very few people ever make use of it.

01:01:49.041 --> 01:01:51.916
Welcome to next year's shortlist.

01:01:53.041 --> 01:01:55.250
You should be proud of yourself, Sarah.

01:01:57.291 --> 01:01:58.250
Thanks.

01:02:01.375 --> 01:02:05.500
Sensational performance from Annunziata.
Confidently overtaking here.

01:02:14.041 --> 01:02:15.250
Yes!

01:02:19.750 --> 01:02:20.750
Hi.

01:02:22.500 --> 01:02:23.458
Good luck.

01:02:25.208 --> 01:02:26.041
Thanks.

01:02:36.750 --> 01:02:39.165
All three are giving it their all today.

01:02:39.166 --> 01:02:42.749
McKinnen, Paulsen and Annunziata,
they are all sensational.

01:02:42.750 --> 01:02:43.875
Who will hold his nerve?

01:02:45.791 --> 01:02:46.958
Will he do it?

01:02:50.541 --> 01:02:52.207
Will he? Will he?

01:02:52.208 --> 01:02:56.790
He overtakes. He's done it.
Annunziata wins on the Alpen Racetrack.

01:02:56.791 --> 01:02:59.750
Sensational! What a finish!

01:03:09.708 --> 01:03:13.249
And this year's Alpen Racetrack champion,

01:03:13.250 --> 01:03:17.958
Dante Annunziata.

01:03:43.208 --> 01:03:45.500
Candidate driver?

01:03:48.458 --> 01:03:49.875
For next year?

01:03:54.583 --> 01:03:55.416
Mom,

01:03:56.416 --> 01:03:59.375
Mr. Bronson is serious about this.
I'm sure of it.

01:04:00.166 --> 01:04:02.207
That, or he's using you.

01:04:02.208 --> 01:04:04.166
Or he's supporting me.

01:04:04.708 --> 01:04:06.875
Why haven't you told me
anything about this?

01:04:09.541 --> 01:04:10.958
And what does Dante say?

01:04:17.541 --> 01:04:18.958
He doesn't know?

01:04:24.333 --> 01:04:27.457
Sweetheart, I can see that
you have feelings for him.

01:04:27.458 --> 01:04:29.458
You have to talk to him.

01:04:34.416 --> 01:04:35.583
I'll get it.

01:04:46.291 --> 01:04:47.125
Hi.

01:04:51.000 --> 01:04:52.333
What are you doing here?

01:04:59.541 --> 01:05:00.541
Irene, right?

01:05:01.291 --> 01:05:02.125
Yes?

01:05:03.000 --> 01:05:04.458
Dante. It's nice to meet you.

01:05:10.958 --> 01:05:13.958
I wanted to… whisk you away.

01:05:19.541 --> 01:05:20.958
What if I don't want to go?

01:05:25.250 --> 01:05:27.333
Then it'll be a case for Interpol.

01:05:32.041 --> 01:05:36.125
We have almost exactly 68 hours
before the dinner with the sponsors.

01:05:37.833 --> 01:05:39.083
We should be okay.

01:06:07.875 --> 01:06:08.958
Can we…

01:07:54.666 --> 01:07:57.916
I'd like to show you something
I've never shown anyone before.

01:08:01.541 --> 01:08:02.375
Okay.

01:08:11.208 --> 01:08:12.832
The day the accident happened,

01:08:12.833 --> 01:08:15.415
we weren't just out for a drive,
like everyone says.

01:08:15.416 --> 01:08:17.166
We were fighting.

01:08:18.583 --> 01:08:22.083
{\an8}Because I thought that she wasn't ready
to go professional.

01:08:42.250 --> 01:08:44.208
I gave her this for her 18th birthday.

01:08:47.416 --> 01:08:49.583
"My angel with the bloody knees."

01:08:52.791 --> 01:08:54.375
That's what Mom always called her.

01:09:06.250 --> 01:09:08.582
Gabriella was very ambitious.

01:09:08.583 --> 01:09:10.333
A talented driver.

01:09:12.625 --> 01:09:14.000
Just like you.

01:09:17.291 --> 01:09:18.875
I didn't believe in her.

01:09:19.916 --> 01:09:21.291
I kept her small.

01:09:22.625 --> 01:09:26.875
And that's what set her off
when she was next to me at the wheel.

01:09:29.208 --> 01:09:31.083
I'll never forget
the way she looked at me.

01:09:36.541 --> 01:09:38.124
She drove off in a frenzy.

01:09:38.125 --> 01:09:40.415
She wanted to prove herself.

01:09:40.416 --> 01:09:41.625
And then, one mistake.

01:09:45.500 --> 01:09:48.750
She loses control of her car
and dies instantly.

01:09:50.166 --> 01:09:51.208
Because of me.

01:10:10.000 --> 01:10:11.625
It's not your fault.

01:10:49.791 --> 01:10:51.916
- Morning.
- Hey.

01:11:16.625 --> 01:11:19.708
What if we just ran away,
when the season's over?

01:11:23.958 --> 01:11:25.125
Where?

01:11:26.083 --> 01:11:27.291
No idea.

01:11:28.916 --> 01:11:31.000
A fair in southern Italy.

01:11:36.041 --> 01:11:36.875
You and me…

01:11:39.666 --> 01:11:40.500
we could run

01:11:43.458 --> 01:11:45.791
a bumper car stand.

01:11:46.500 --> 01:11:48.000
That sounds nice.

01:12:55.583 --> 01:12:56.875
Do we really have to go?

01:12:59.416 --> 01:13:01.750
We have a contract. Or did you forget?

01:13:02.791 --> 01:13:04.666
In two days, it'll all be over.

01:13:08.375 --> 01:13:09.375
Yeah.

01:13:15.083 --> 01:13:16.416
Dante, I have to tell you…

01:13:27.666 --> 01:13:28.625
Hey, here they are.

01:13:29.625 --> 01:13:30.708
There they are!

01:13:35.125 --> 01:13:36.499
Our guests of honor.

01:13:36.500 --> 01:13:38.916
Come here, big guy. Great to see you.

01:13:42.833 --> 01:13:43.749
Yes.

01:13:43.750 --> 01:13:47.166
It doesn't hurt to ask,
that's all I'm saying.

01:13:52.916 --> 01:13:54.833
But only after changing the tires.

01:13:56.916 --> 01:13:57.916
Okay.

01:13:58.916 --> 01:14:00.875
Oh, my God.

01:14:09.583 --> 01:14:11.083
I'm gonna use the restroom.

01:14:23.916 --> 01:14:25.208
What's up, spare?

01:14:25.791 --> 01:14:27.000
Hey, champ.

01:14:28.000 --> 01:14:30.875
It's probably no big deal, but…

01:14:32.000 --> 01:14:34.750
Was it you who drove
the new best time on Eagle Track?

01:14:38.375 --> 01:14:39.208
During the day?

01:14:40.000 --> 01:14:41.958
Yeah, during the day.

01:14:44.916 --> 01:14:45.833
That's funny.

01:14:56.500 --> 01:15:00.957
Someone breaks your record in the
dead of night, and no one says anything.

01:15:00.958 --> 01:15:04.165
Strange, isn't it?
Not a word from the team.

01:15:04.166 --> 01:15:05.125
It wasn't me.

01:15:06.833 --> 01:15:07.833
Who was it?

01:15:12.208 --> 01:15:13.583
I like this wine.

01:15:14.875 --> 01:15:15.791
Hey, Jack!

01:15:17.791 --> 01:15:21.250
Ruben here thinks
that someone broke my record in the night.

01:15:23.250 --> 01:15:24.291
Who was it?

01:15:31.583 --> 01:15:33.541
I'd like to know that, too.

01:15:41.583 --> 01:15:43.875
Okay, I…

01:15:44.958 --> 01:15:48.625
We didn't want to throw off
your concentration, Dante, okay?

01:15:49.416 --> 01:15:52.875
This close to the season finale,
you and your performance are the priority.

01:15:54.375 --> 01:15:56.708
That's why Sarah and I didn't tell you.

01:15:59.083 --> 01:16:00.291
Didn't tell me what?

01:16:03.000 --> 01:16:04.791
Sarah drove the new best time.

01:16:08.583 --> 01:16:12.957
She was incredibly fast. I've never seen
anything like it in training.

01:16:12.958 --> 01:16:13.833
In training?

01:16:15.958 --> 01:16:17.333
Yeah.

01:16:19.250 --> 01:16:20.249
With you?

01:16:20.250 --> 01:16:25.000
Does that mean we're thinking that Sarah
might become a driver?

01:16:27.250 --> 01:16:28.166
Dante…

01:16:30.333 --> 01:16:31.666
Dante, I…

01:16:35.458 --> 01:16:36.915
Dante, wait.

01:16:36.916 --> 01:16:38.208
Wait.

01:16:40.000 --> 01:16:41.791
- I wanted to tell you.
- What?

01:16:43.291 --> 01:16:45.499
That Jack has been training you in secret?

01:16:45.500 --> 01:16:48.791
That they want to go behind my back
and make you an Eagle driver?

01:16:50.000 --> 01:16:51.666
It's in case you leave.

01:16:54.416 --> 01:16:56.291
You've been playing me for a fool.

01:17:01.458 --> 01:17:02.291
Yes.

01:17:03.375 --> 01:17:05.333
Yes, I've been lying to you.

01:17:06.416 --> 01:17:10.750
But this is my big chance.
Bronson's giving me an opportunity.

01:17:11.625 --> 01:17:13.708
- That means more to me than…
- Than I do?

01:17:15.833 --> 01:17:17.582
Is that what you're trying to say?

01:17:17.583 --> 01:17:19.125
No, of course not, but…

01:17:22.875 --> 01:17:25.791
I couldn't have known
that I'd fall in love with you.

01:17:27.833 --> 01:17:31.666
After this race,
our business relationship is over.

01:17:33.458 --> 01:17:35.833
You get your money
and I'll get some peace.

01:17:37.708 --> 01:17:38.708
Yes.

01:17:46.958 --> 01:17:48.041
Dante.

01:18:52.625 --> 01:18:55.540
What kind of spectacle
are we in for today?

01:18:55.541 --> 01:19:01.374
80,000 tickets have been sold for the
German Grand Prix, the Euro Masters,

01:19:01.375 --> 01:19:04.582
here in Donnersbach,
on the traditional track.

01:19:04.583 --> 01:19:09.832
Yesterday, we saw the teams put together
a very exciting qualifying session.

01:19:09.833 --> 01:19:15.416
Jakatomi, McKinnen and Annunziata
all have a shot at the title.

01:19:16.208 --> 01:19:20.540
Annunziata is in pole position, leading
the pack, and he has set the fastest time.

01:19:20.541 --> 01:19:24.540
He had a very strong qualifying session,
and showed nerves of steel.

01:19:24.541 --> 01:19:27.415
But everything hinges on today.

01:19:27.416 --> 01:19:32.249
This story is being written live.
Nothing is decided yet.

01:19:32.250 --> 01:19:36.082
And it's that uncertainty
that makes this sport so attractive.

01:19:36.083 --> 01:19:40.958
Who can clinch the victory, here and now?
Who is going to do it?

01:20:04.416 --> 01:20:07.000
We could always
keep declining the interview.

01:20:07.666 --> 01:20:08.500
Why?

01:20:09.250 --> 01:20:10.708
It's part of the job.

01:20:17.958 --> 01:20:20.583
Okay, in that case we need to go.

01:20:21.125 --> 01:20:21.958
Right?

01:20:29.000 --> 01:20:30.707
Hello, Irene.

01:20:30.708 --> 01:20:32.082
Ruben?

01:20:32.083 --> 01:20:33.499
Long time.

01:20:33.500 --> 01:20:34.750
It's been forever.

01:20:36.250 --> 01:20:37.291
Is everything okay?

01:20:39.708 --> 01:20:41.499
Sarah's left already, right?

01:20:41.500 --> 01:20:42.666
Yes.

01:20:43.291 --> 01:20:44.791
Has something happened?

01:20:46.333 --> 01:20:47.750
Can I come in?

01:20:49.000 --> 01:20:51.832
Tell me, why can't Sarah know
that you're here?

01:20:51.833 --> 01:20:55.125
Because she feels that
she can handle things on her own.

01:20:57.375 --> 01:21:00.082
Lately, I haven't been able
to get through to her at all.

01:21:00.083 --> 01:21:03.207
And that's exactly why we need
to help her out of this.

01:21:03.208 --> 01:21:05.249
These people only think about themselves.

01:21:05.250 --> 01:21:08.166
They will drop her the moment
she stops being useful to them.

01:21:08.875 --> 01:21:11.041
They did the same with me.

01:21:17.458 --> 01:21:20.666
I told her from the start
that this deal wouldn't end well.

01:21:22.000 --> 01:21:23.708
What deal?

01:21:31.166 --> 01:21:32.625
Look.

01:21:35.333 --> 01:21:40.290
They're offering her 200,000 euros
to pretend to be Dante's fiancée.

01:21:40.291 --> 01:21:42.583
- Weird, right?
- For sure.

01:21:46.708 --> 01:21:47.541
See there.

01:21:52.541 --> 01:21:56.124
She forbade me
from talking to anyone about it.

01:21:56.125 --> 01:21:57.916
Sure, this is explosive.

01:21:58.541 --> 01:22:00.250
Not a word to anybody.

01:22:01.041 --> 01:22:03.082
- Hello. Yes.
- Great to see you.

01:22:03.083 --> 01:22:04.915
Nice to meet you, hello.

01:22:04.916 --> 01:22:06.250
Hello.

01:22:07.416 --> 01:22:10.540
- Please sit back there.
- Thank you.

01:22:10.541 --> 01:22:12.500
I think that's a good spot.

01:22:14.500 --> 01:22:15.707
How lovely.

01:22:15.708 --> 01:22:17.875
I'm very excited to have you here.

01:22:19.500 --> 01:22:21.333
We're excited to be here.

01:22:22.291 --> 01:22:27.207
Dante, what is going through your head
in the moments before this big finale?

01:22:27.208 --> 01:22:28.915
Not a lot.

01:22:28.916 --> 01:22:30.166
Oh, please.

01:22:31.708 --> 01:22:35.583
No, honestly.
I'm totally focused on the race.

01:22:36.250 --> 01:22:38.666
Totally focused on the race.

01:22:40.208 --> 01:22:44.624
You two have turned
into a regular power couple.

01:22:44.625 --> 01:22:48.500
How are you feeling about that, Sarah?

01:22:49.291 --> 01:22:51.624
All this attention all of a sudden.

01:22:51.625 --> 01:22:54.500
Your world is quite different
from Dante's.

01:22:59.208 --> 01:23:00.541
I was…

01:23:02.500 --> 01:23:04.208
I am just…

01:23:07.166 --> 01:23:11.415
I am just very grateful for everything
we have experienced together.

01:23:11.416 --> 01:23:13.333
What you have done with me.

01:23:17.500 --> 01:23:18.666
Sorry.

01:23:19.833 --> 01:23:22.749
Thanks to him, my world has changed a lot.

01:23:22.750 --> 01:23:28.082
The mechanic. The racing driver.
Such great happiness.

01:23:28.083 --> 01:23:29.500
You could say that.

01:23:30.416 --> 01:23:32.541
It sounds like a modern-day fairy tale.

01:23:34.041 --> 01:23:39.416
And we all know what
good fairy tales need.

01:23:40.333 --> 01:23:41.750
A good script.

01:23:45.125 --> 01:23:47.832
Or a water-tight contract.

01:23:47.833 --> 01:23:50.207
It's all written in here. Every word.

01:23:50.208 --> 01:23:53.999
Affection, kiss, discretion.

01:23:54.000 --> 01:23:57.082
- Stop. Excuse me. Could we…
- And your name, right next to Sarah's.

01:23:57.083 --> 01:23:59.957
- Stop, can we cut?
- Is this love?

01:23:59.958 --> 01:24:01.915
- Or just…
- Can I see that?

01:24:01.916 --> 01:24:06.249
Okay, I know someone who
knows about this kind of thing.

01:24:06.250 --> 01:24:08.540
I could take some photos
and send them to him,

01:24:08.541 --> 01:24:10.457
just to be on the safe side, okay?

01:24:10.458 --> 01:24:11.375
Okay.

01:24:14.583 --> 01:24:18.833
Or is it all just a well-staged deal?

01:24:19.458 --> 01:24:22.083
Dear viewers, stay tuned.

01:24:23.916 --> 01:24:25.875
Fuck. What a pile of shit.

01:24:26.500 --> 01:24:28.874
- Where are you going?
- To race.

01:24:28.875 --> 01:24:30.166
Shit.

01:24:31.000 --> 01:24:33.540
Shit, fucking shit.

01:24:33.541 --> 01:24:36.290
Interesting developments
just minutes from the start.

01:24:36.291 --> 01:24:39.415
Dante Annunziata and Team Eagle
have been accused

01:24:39.416 --> 01:24:41.624
of faking his relationship
with Sarah Jenkins

01:24:41.625 --> 01:24:43.875
{\an8}to squash the scandal around the photo.

01:24:47.583 --> 01:24:48.874
One moment.

01:24:48.875 --> 01:24:50.708
You want to drive?

01:24:51.375 --> 01:24:52.416
I want to win.

01:24:53.291 --> 01:24:56.375
That's it. That's it.
Exactly right. Go and win it.

01:24:57.791 --> 01:25:01.124
Yes, and will these accusations
have an effect on Annunziata?

01:25:01.125 --> 01:25:04.083
His private life is a constant
source of turmoil.

01:25:13.791 --> 01:25:18.165
Sweetie, I'm so sorry.
Ruben was here. He said he wanted to help.

01:25:18.166 --> 01:25:21.124
He took pictures of the contract.
He must be behind this.

01:25:21.125 --> 01:25:22.000
What?

01:25:26.500 --> 01:25:27.541
There you are.

01:25:30.541 --> 01:25:31.375
Why?

01:25:32.958 --> 01:25:34.583
Why did you do it?

01:25:36.500 --> 01:25:37.500
Why?

01:25:39.416 --> 01:25:44.208
Because I've been working my ass off
for this team for four years!

01:25:46.083 --> 01:25:47.500
And what do I get?

01:25:49.666 --> 01:25:53.874
Bronson should have fired him for
that photo of you two in the locker room.

01:25:53.875 --> 01:25:57.791
Instead, he can keep driving, and he gets…

01:26:01.708 --> 01:26:02.583
you?

01:26:06.833 --> 01:26:08.083
It was you.

01:26:16.500 --> 01:26:18.041
- Sarah, I…
- No.

01:26:23.458 --> 01:26:24.500
Fuck you, Ruben.

01:26:26.833 --> 01:26:29.041
You just weren't fast enough.

01:26:44.875 --> 01:26:46.250
Hello. Thank you.

01:26:49.250 --> 01:26:51.540
- It surely can't get any worse today.
- No.

01:26:51.541 --> 01:26:53.707
Great atmosphere here in Donnersbach.

01:26:53.708 --> 01:26:57.415
The fans here are
almost as keyed-up as the drivers.

01:26:57.416 --> 01:27:00.625
Okay, and now go get the title.
It belongs to you.

01:27:09.333 --> 01:27:13.666
It's nearly time now. The grand finale
to a truly thrilling season.

01:27:24.958 --> 01:27:27.957
Doing well out of the straight,
Annunziata takes the lead,

01:27:27.958 --> 01:27:30.125
aggressive driving from the get-go.

01:27:33.375 --> 01:27:34.541
Yeah!

01:27:46.125 --> 01:27:49.915
Lap 15. Annunziata is
confidently building up his lead.

01:27:49.916 --> 01:27:53.541
He's now got a 12-second lead
over Paulsen in second place.

01:28:01.041 --> 01:28:03.374
Okay, pit lane, Dante!
Your tires are worn.

01:28:03.375 --> 01:28:04.957
No, not yet!

01:28:04.958 --> 01:28:06.957
Dante, the tires are about to blow.

01:28:06.958 --> 01:28:08.291
Your race, your call.

01:28:16.958 --> 01:28:17.916
No.

01:28:22.291 --> 01:28:25.624
21st lap. Suddenly Annunziata's car skids.

01:28:25.625 --> 01:28:28.707
What's this? Contact with the barriers.
Totally unnecessary.

01:28:28.708 --> 01:28:31.790
What's up with Annunziata?
Is it his nerves or is it the tires?

01:28:31.791 --> 01:28:34.290
He's the only driver
not to have changed tires yet.

01:28:34.291 --> 01:28:37.332
Yes, a very questionable strategy decision
for Eagle Racing.

01:28:37.333 --> 01:28:38.625
I'm coming in.

01:28:56.000 --> 01:28:57.000
Dante, what's up?

01:28:58.375 --> 01:28:59.540
Dante?

01:28:59.541 --> 01:29:01.625
I… I can't do it.

01:29:02.166 --> 01:29:04.207
What can't you do? What's wrong?

01:29:04.208 --> 01:29:07.624
What do you mean, you can't?
You're in the lead!

01:29:07.625 --> 01:29:10.040
Is this the turning point
for Eagle Racing?

01:29:10.041 --> 01:29:13.041
His lead is evaporating!
Annunziata isn't leaving the pit.

01:29:16.291 --> 01:29:17.250
Hey!

01:29:19.000 --> 01:29:19.833
Dante.

01:29:25.375 --> 01:29:26.333
Do it for her.

01:29:27.458 --> 01:29:29.958
Do it for the angel with the bloody knees.

01:29:34.250 --> 01:29:35.833
Dante, what's going on? Drive!

01:29:40.375 --> 01:29:44.332
Annunziata is back in the race!
Paulsen's in first, Jakatomi in second.

01:29:44.333 --> 01:29:47.291
What a thriller.
This finale is always tense.

01:29:54.041 --> 01:29:58.083
Annunziata working bravely on the outside.
A world-class overtaking maneu…

01:30:16.083 --> 01:30:17.666
Four seconds to Paulsen.

01:30:24.541 --> 01:30:26.291
Two seconds to Paulsen.

01:30:38.666 --> 01:30:39.708
Do it!

01:31:45.833 --> 01:31:48.540
He's done it! It's crazy!

01:31:48.541 --> 01:31:49.540
Yes! Yes!

01:31:49.541 --> 01:31:53.332
Annunziata wins the German Grand Prix
in Donnersbach.

01:31:53.333 --> 01:31:55.583
Against all odds! Incredible!

01:32:12.250 --> 01:32:15.208
You did it, son! You did it!

01:32:18.208 --> 01:32:19.666
You did it!

01:32:20.458 --> 01:32:22.125
You did it, Dante.

01:32:22.875 --> 01:32:24.791
- Dante.
- We did it.

01:32:26.375 --> 01:32:28.416
We did it. We did it.

01:33:08.375 --> 01:33:12.583
Dante Annunziata!

01:33:24.500 --> 01:33:25.416
Sarah!

01:33:28.041 --> 01:33:29.083
Sarah!

01:33:30.291 --> 01:33:32.665
I was just up on the podium,

01:33:32.666 --> 01:33:35.166
but for the first time ever,
I didn't care.

01:33:36.500 --> 01:33:38.624
I just wanted to be here.

01:33:38.625 --> 01:33:39.625
With you.

01:34:06.083 --> 01:34:06.916
Now what?

01:34:07.875 --> 01:34:09.125
Do we drive off?

01:34:10.416 --> 01:34:11.250
Why not?

01:34:14.583 --> 01:34:15.541
You drive.

01:34:23.791 --> 01:34:24.916
Okay, hop in!

01:34:28.291 --> 01:34:30.832
So, people,
at first, it was a fake love story

01:34:30.833 --> 01:34:32.665
and then it turned into real love.

01:34:32.666 --> 01:34:35.707
I knew all along that it was for real.

01:34:35.708 --> 01:34:37.624
Their love never seemed fake to me.

01:34:37.625 --> 01:34:39.540
It was real the whole time.

01:34:39.541 --> 01:34:42.790
Is this true love,
or just a contractual requirement?

01:34:42.791 --> 01:34:45.750
People, where are Sarah and Dante?

01:34:56.083 --> 01:34:56.958
Sarah, hi!

01:34:57.375 --> 01:34:59.999
I've been trying to reach you for days.
Where are you?

01:35:00.000 --> 01:35:04.749
If, by chance, you're still alive and
interested in your career, listen to me.

01:35:04.750 --> 01:35:08.374
We want you, not as a marketing gimmick,
but as a driver.

01:35:08.375 --> 01:35:09.957
Eagle's new number one.

01:35:09.958 --> 01:35:12.082
I haven't heard from Dante. Just rumors.

01:35:12.083 --> 01:35:14.874
An offer from Formula 1 maybe.
Whatever. Don't care.

01:35:14.875 --> 01:35:17.665
It's about you now.
This is your big chance.

01:35:17.666 --> 01:35:19.375
Call me back. We need to talk.

01:35:29.916 --> 01:35:30.750
Hey.

01:35:32.916 --> 01:35:35.041
I think you should accept.

01:35:40.791 --> 01:35:41.875
What about you?

01:35:43.333 --> 01:35:45.540
Maybe I don't want to do Formula 1 anymore

01:35:45.541 --> 01:35:47.416
after you've signed.

01:35:48.833 --> 01:35:51.332
- And instead?
- I stay and look forward

01:35:51.333 --> 01:35:52.791
to seeing your pretty smile…

01:35:53.416 --> 01:35:54.708
in the rearview mirror.

01:35:57.416 --> 01:35:58.458
You wish.